{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GryGR4gmW4G9AaHApqe8jd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#pragma once\n2\t#include \"lzma_packet.h\"\n3\t#include \"lzma_state.h\"\n4\t#include \"packet_enumerator.h\"\n5\t#include <stdbool.h>\n6\t\n7\t//The Top-K packet finder will iterate all possible next packets given an input LZMAState. It will construct a list of size K of the packets that produce in the highest compression ratio. This list can then be iterated over by calling \"pop\", which pops off the worst element in the list. the last element popped will be the best element\n8\t\n9\ttypedef struct TopKPacketFinder_struct TopKPacketFinder;\n10\t\n11\tTopKPacketFinder* top_k_packet_finder_new(size_t size, const PacketEnumerator* packet_enumerator);\n12\tvoid top_k_packet_finder_free(TopKPacketFinder* finder);\n13\t\n14\tsize_t top_k_packet_finder_count(const TopKPacketFinder* finder);\n15\t//todo: remove the next_packets thing because I think it only causes hardship.. or maybe we should abstract-out the cost function\n16\tvoid top_k_packet_finder_find(TopKPacketFinder* finder, const LZMAState* lzma_state, LZMAPacket* next_packets);\n17\t\n18\tbool top_k_packet_finder_pop(TopKPacketFinder* finder, LZMAPacket* packet);\n19\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"623375f8-b149-44ba-a89c-aa2806c1bc79","uuid":"2f51d366-a38a-400c-89ac-9d8c2771b49c","timestamp":"2026-06-06T04:14:48.269Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-31062124/harvest-crust-twDuq5/project/c_src/src/top_k_packet_finder.h","content":"#pragma once\n#include \"lzma_packet.h\"\n#include \"lzma_state.h\"\n#include \"packet_enumerator.h\"\n#include <stdbool.h>\n\n//The Top-K packet finder will iterate all possible next packets given an input LZMAState. It will construct a list of size K of the packets that produce in the highest compression ratio. This list can then be iterated over by calling \"pop\", which pops off the worst element in the list. the last element popped will be the best element\n\ntypedef struct TopKPacketFinder_struct TopKPacketFinder;\n\nTopKPacketFinder* top_k_packet_finder_new(size_t size, const PacketEnumerator* packet_enumerator);\nvoid top_k_packet_finder_free(TopKPacketFinder* finder);\n\nsize_t top_k_packet_finder_count(const TopKPacketFinder* finder);\n//todo: remove the next_packets thing because I think it only causes hardship.. or maybe we should abstract-out the cost function\nvoid top_k_packet_finder_find(TopKPacketFinder* finder, const LZMAState* lzma_state, LZMAPacket* next_packets);\n\nbool top_k_packet_finder_pop(TopKPacketFinder* finder, LZMAPacket* packet);\n","numLines":19,"startLine":1,"totalLines":19}}}
